From 3a8efbf9d689fe47041b98b97dce30ec38b35216 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PGMaps trial <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:17:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] scatter: fixed instances; example: a PGMaps forest scene

PlacementRules.instances takes a fixed list (x, z, yaw, width scale,
height scale) in place of blue-noise points, so an existing inventory
can be drawn with the scatter's streaming, levels of detail and
impostors. Tiles take the instances inside them; a new list regenerates
them (keyed by identity, never serialised). Optional, so every existing
layer is unchanged.

example/pgmaps-scene.html draws a PGMaps forest scene package: the
package's ground, its stems as fixed instances on B.C. species built
from the spruce, pine, fir and birch presets with PGMaps' crown bases,
its slash, and its camera. &still stops on a streamed-in frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
